        "original_id": "ea41cce6-df49-58a1-b1b1-821589188c15",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Seasons\n- People: Marius Petipa, Alexander Glazunov\n- Organizations: Saint Petersburg Conservatory, Petrograd Conservatory, Leningrad Conservatory\n- Concepts: ballet, choreography, music, Bolshevik Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- The Seasons is an allegorical ballet in one act and four scenes.\n- The Seasons was choreographed by Marius Petipa.\n- The Seasons features music by Alexander Glazunov.\n- Between 1905 and 1928, Alexander Glazunov served as director of the Saint Petersburg Conservatory.\n- Following the Bolshevik Revolution, Alexander Glazunov was instrumental in reorganizing the Saint Petersburg Conservatory into the Petrograd Conservatory and then the Leningrad Conservatory.",
